# Design System

Purpose: single source of truth for the HOSSPI HMS visual system.

## Mandatory rules

- Use Material 3 as the default foundation.
- Light theme is the default; support dark theme and system theme mode.
- Light theme: clean blue-based palette; dark theme: clean, readable, Material-aligned.
- Do not hard-code colors, spacing, radius, elevation, or typography in feature widgets.
- Store theme mode as a non-sensitive preference when persisted.
- Theme changes must update the app reactively.
- Shared components read colors, typography, shape, and spacing from the active theme or design tokens.

## Token access (mandatory)

Read tokens through theme extensions — do not duplicate numeric constants in features:

```dart
final theme = Theme.of(context);
theme.spacing.md;           // AppSpacingTokens via app_theme_extensions
theme.appTokens;            // AppDesignTokens
theme.colorScheme.primary;  // ColorScheme roles
```

- Use `theme.textTheme` for typography — not inline `TextStyle(fontSize: 14, ...)`.
- Use `AppWorkspaceStatusTone` / semantic status colors from theme extensions for status chips — not ad-hoc `Colors.green`.
- Use `AppFormatters` / `app_formatters.dart` for currency and dates — not manual string building.

## Color standard

| Theme | Baseline |
|---|---|
| Light | `ColorScheme.fromSeed(seedColor: Color(0xFF1565C0), brightness: Brightness.light)` |
| Dark | `ColorScheme.fromSeed(seedColor: Color(0xFF90CAF9), brightness: Brightness.dark)` |
| Error | Material error roles from active `ColorScheme` |
| Status | success, warning, info via theme extension only when required |

## Design tokens

| Token group | Values |
|---|---|
| Spacing | `xs=4`, `sm=8`, `md=12`, `lg=16`, `xl=24`, `xxl=32` |
| Radius | `none=0`, `xs=4`, `sm=8`, `md=10`, `lg=12`, `xl=16`, `xxl=24`, `full=pill/circular` (open scale — no upper cap) |
| Page padding | mobile `16`, tablet `24`, desktop `32` |
| Button height | compact `36–40`, standard `40–48` |
| Icon size | default `20–24`; larger only when layout requires |
| Max widths | see [`layouts.mdc`](./layouts.mdc) |

## Shape and density

- Corner radii have no fixed cap: choose any radius token (`xs`…`xxl`, or `full` for pill/circular) that suits the surface. There is no mandated `8–12` range.
- Always source radii from `theme.radius` tokens; do not hard-code numeric radii in feature widgets.
- Radii must be responsive: derive them via `context.responsiveRadius(theme.radius.<token>)` (or `AppRadiusTokens.responsive`) so they scale down on compact screens and up on large desktops.
- Rely on `RoundedRectangleBorder`/`BorderRadius` auto-clamping (radius is limited to half the shortest side) so large radii never overflow small controls.
- Avoid excessive padding; keep desktop controls visually balanced.
- Use consistent elevation and borders; keep the shape language uniform across related card/button/dialog styles.
- Keep navigation items readable without oversized icons or row heights.

## Typography

- Use theme text styles, not raw duplicated `TextStyle`.
- Keep headings consistent by screen purpose.
- Keep body text readable at scaled font sizes.
- Use locale-aware text direction where needed.

